# Line endings.
#
# This repo is worked on from Windows (desktop + laptop) and Linux. Without a
# rule, Git's core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites line endings on checkout,
# which can make a one-line change look like the whole file changed and can
# create conflicts that are pure whitespace.
#
# text=auto  — treat text files as text and store them with LF in the repo
# eol=lf     — check them out as LF everywhere, so no machine rewrites them
#
# Python, Git Bash, and modern Windows editors all handle LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.db binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
